    {
      "id": "AGF-03",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-adelic-gram-orbit",
      "title": "The whole regular Gram fibre is one adelic orbit",
      "statement": "For a rational tuple X of nonsingular Gram matrix T and any compact set of adelic tuples Ω, a single compact subset of the adelic unitary group carries X to every tuple in Ω with Gram matrix T. A common finite set of primes suffices for the integrality of the representatives and their inverses.",
      "hypotheses": "The base is a number field, the coefficient field is its CM quadratic extension, and the ambient Hermitian form is nonsingular. Use the restricted product topology and the matrix-and-inverse topology on the group.",
      "dependencies": [
        "AGF-02"
      ],
      "equations": [],
